    explanation: 'The application core defines "ports," which are interfaces describing what it needs (e.g. a PaymentGateway port) or offers (e.g. an OrderService port), without knowing about HTTP, databases, or message brokers. "Adapters" implement those ports for specific technologies: a REST controller is a driving/primary adapter, while a Postgres repository or Stripe client is a driven/secondary adapter. This symmetry between input and output adapters is the key difference from a simple layered approach, and it makes it trivial to swap a REST adapter for a CLI or test double without touching core logic. It is especially useful when the same business logic must be exposed via multiple entry points (API, queue consumer, scheduled job).',
